  "decision": "FAIL / NO_CANDIDATE_ADMITTED / NO_ROBUST_FACTOR_PASS. F-SLOOS-STANDARDS showed some timing value relative to its availability-matched unconditional half-retention control: on the preregistered 2010-05-01+ window candidate Sharpe 1.295631 exceeded matched-control Sharpe 1.279036, candidate MDD 8.573895% stayed below 10%, and 4/6 fixed folds matched or beat the control. However, candidate CAGR 11.881307% was below V11 12.032638% and candidate Sharpe remained below V11 1.379309. Paired 63-session moving-block bootstrap over 20,000 replicates gave P(CAGR candidate > V11)=36.025% and P(Sharpe candidate > matched)=77.975%; median candidate-minus-V11 CAGR was negative while median candidate-minus-matched Sharpe was positive. Bootstrap MDD P97.5 was 14.947%, within the frozen 15% ceiling, but cumulative 33-trial DSR probability was only 92.204%. The factor therefore contains at most weak incremental timing information and does not qualify as a robust return source. Per the frozen stop rule, no threshold, sign, survey variant, persistence, retention-fraction, event-definition, asset-scope, or gross-target rescue is permitted.",
